  "core_idea": "**Whoever** means **who**, with the added idea that it could be any person at all, or, in questions, that the speaker is surprised.",
  "senses": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "any person who",
      "definition": "the person who, or any person who",
      "explanation": "**Whoever** begins a clause that acts like a noun phrase: *whoever finishes first* is the person who finishes first. It is used both when the person is not known (*whoever took my umbrella*) and when it could be anyone (*invite whoever you like*). When **whoever** is the subject of its own clause, that verb is singular: *whoever wins*.",
      "grammar": {
        "countability": null,
        "transitivity": null,
        "codes": [],
        "patterns": []
      },
